# tools/conformance/css_property_suite.py: the property vectors of web-platform-tests' css/ that fail because the library is wrong or
# incomplete: the page is right (and, for a serialization, both browsers write what the page writes), the library is not. One line a
# case. Columns (tab separated): vector (file#n), property, value, stage, the answer the library gives, owner (the piece of work that
# closes it), and what the library lacks. A defect is never allowed to stay: the number listed has a ceiling (CSS_PROPERTY_MAX_DEFECTS in
# the Makefile) that only goes down, and a case that the library passes now has to be removed from here (a stale line fails).
# Owners: canonical-serialization (the specified value is written in its shortest or normalized form), grammar (the grammar of the
# property or of a type it names accepts or refuses what the draft does not), function-types (a function the library implements in code
# does not take a form the draft gives it), pin (the pinned data lacks or words differently what the draft says), values (a value
# layer feature: math functions, substitution, url modifiers), shorthand (the expansion or the writing back of a shorthand: the shorthand layer
# lacks something about the shorthand that the page has).
